WEBVTT

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.570
<b>I tried coming alone to our usual park.</b>

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.070
<b>It's a feeling I've never felt.</b>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:21.660
<b>Like a child, frightened by the sound of the wind</b>

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.670
<b>I ran back along the path home.</b>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.970
<b>The sky outside the window is too vast. Where are you now?</b>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.130
<b>Please, may this reach you...</b>

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:44.690
<b>Dear Lord, if you ever grant wishes,</b>

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.110
<b>grant my wish right now, please!</b>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>I want to hear your voice, I miss you! I want to see you now!</b>

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.830
<b>Why must you already be looking toward tomorrow?</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:06.210
<b>Don't just brush it off, saying the time has slipped by.</b>

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>Once more...</b>

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:14.550
<b>I love you, and yet it's been too late since long ago.</b>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.140
<b>Even if I give up, it can't be like the past.</b>

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Don't just decide so simply there's no way, no choice.</b>

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.230
<b>Smile once more.</b>

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.500
How long is this going to take?

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.980
While we're wasting time 
here, the guy's escaping!

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.780
I-I wouldn't be worried about Holly, though. 

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.450
That guy's probably seriously 
regretting it by now.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.140
Bet he never counted on 
grabbing someone so violent.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.520
Stop going on about my sister like that.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.640
I'm not in the mood for joking around.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:09.570
Yeah...

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.770
Nothing's changed.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.820
We haven't discovered in what 
direction they escaped to.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.910
The only clue we have is your testimony.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.920
The criminal is a guy with red eyes!

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.220
And he escaped after grabbing Holly!

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.090
A guy with red eyes?

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.000
I have something I'd like 
you to confirm for me.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:29.870
That's...

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:35.700
We're in pursuit of a man that's 
caused a series of incidents.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.330
The man you encountered...

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.400
He seemed similar, but...

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.260
I can't be sure...

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.220
I see.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.500
I don't know what exactly is going 
on, but we may need your help.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.440
If we make any progress, we'll contact you.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:57.250
Joey, don't get down on yourself.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.320
I won't...

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:07.830
Will...

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.530
What the heck are you doing?

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:30.000
It's no use. The files about 
the incidents won't open.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.230
And I thought we might get a clue if we 
searched through the Professor's computer.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:37.230
Do you think Will is responsible?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.010
Of course not!

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:42.110
That guy's not gonna go 
around attacking people.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.450
I don't know, but he seemed really similar.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.560
Could it be that he's been completely 
taken over by the Skrugg?

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.010
You're seriously doubting him?

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.400
You're nuts.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.250
That guy is never gonna do 
something that'd hurt people.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.030
Did you forget already?

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:00.510
He attacked us before to 
get back the Skrugg weapon.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.130
My sister might also...

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.900
This is completely different than before!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.600
How can you be so sure of that?

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.250
Calm down.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.390
You getting all upset is just 
going to make things worse.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:20.160
What's important now is finding Holly, 
not worrying about who's responsible.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.410
I know.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.580
But, how?

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.720
Soil? Why?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.330
These are the samples the 
Professor was researching.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.010
And the place they were taken 
from is written on them.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.500
So that's where he hid them?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.470
He said that the soil was a witness 
to the incidents... Is that true?

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:59.760
He also said something about 
"they're all connected..."

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.900
Where was he heading?

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:07.050
Maybe there is some connection 
between all the different places.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.090
What's the X?

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:21.400
That is definitely a fascinating analysis.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:27.470
Our science team has discovered an unknown 
element in the soil samples Matthew Denton took.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.660
We call it "Component X."

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.290
It's the reason the plants 
in the area had dried up.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:37.260
Then that suspect really 
is connected to the Skrugg?

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.950
I don't know that yet.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:43.270
But it might be a clue 
to our culprit's hideout.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:44.440
Agent Hughes.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.060
Please take a look at the main monitor.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:53.580
That's...

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.950
I've plotted the places where the 
soil samples were taken on the map.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.630
Then, taking into account the concentration 
of Component X found in each location...

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.650
The soil contamination fans out like this...

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:07.710
And the origin?

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.300
In the northeast industrial 
sector... A mountain range.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.330
There's an abandoned mine.

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.060
I see.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.690
No better place to hide than that.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:33.060
Matthew Denton's van has been found 
on the road at the foot of the mine.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:37.230
Thanks to your quick thinking, 
we've got the trail of the culprit.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.250
That's quite impressive work.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.540
I understand your feelings,

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.870
but it's possible that we're up 
against a remnant of the Skrugg.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:51.180
If you let your personal feelings get in 
the way, you're putting your life at risk.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.090
Yeah, you don't need to tell us that.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.650
Fine, then.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:00.720
We will need Heroman and your 
cooperation for this plan.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.560
Especially you, Joey.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.740
You probably know the inside 
of that coal mine very well.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:11.810
The operation starts in one hour. 
We'll finish this before sunrise.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:39.840
Still worried about him?

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.000
I don't know what I should do.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.940
I'll fight anyone if it's for my sister.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.640
Even if it's Will...

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:56.410
But... Then, Lina would...

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.300
I thought I'd made up my mind...

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.720
If you hesitate the ball will 
get taken away from you...

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:20.490
You learn that when you 
play football like I used to.

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:23.380
Will and I were always on the same team.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:28.470
I was the running back and 
he was the quarterback.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:33.710
We were great teammates... Whenever our 
eyes met, we'd face off like a scrimmage...

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.160
What the hell do you think you're doing?

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.140
Why didn't you go where I told you?

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.710
I got results, so what's your problem?

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:47.590
I am the captain!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.290
You trying to make me look like a chump?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.340
I thought you wanted to become 
a victorious hero, right?

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:56.060
Stop being such a stubborn 
fool and throw me the ball!

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.870
I'll put this game away!

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.240
Set! Hut!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:30.210
Psy, I'm givin' you the 
ball just like you wanted!

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.360
You idiot!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.380
Throw it right!

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.510
All right!

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.900
It was strange...

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.620
My leg hurt so bad, even though I was
supposed to have lost all feeling in it.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:37.280
I wanted to run again... I wanted to 
score a touchdown, one more time...

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:42.110
But with this leg, I'll never 
run on the field again...

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.260
Even though I knew it was an 
accident I invited upon myself,

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:48.150
I couldn't forgive Will.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.280
I found out later.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:21.510
He resigned as Captain.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:26.820
I think he suffered just as much as I did.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.000
Will can definitely got on your nerves.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:36.290
But I realize this now.

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:40.800
He's not someone that can go hurting 
other people and live with it.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.930
It's not him that kidnapped Holly, understand?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.430
I believe you, Psy.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.170
You're really going inside?

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:16.830
Yeah. This is our revenge match.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.170
We're gonna bring back 
Holly and the Professor!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:20.850
Yeah!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.860
What's with this place?

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.560
It's all damp and burning hot.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.340
It wasn't like this before...

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.500
These are Prof. Denton's glasses!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.850
Bingo!

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.000
The Professor and Holly must be in here!

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:13.220
Let's hurry.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:36.780
What in the world...

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.490
Joey, look at that!

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:44.000
The culprit is gathering everyone here!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:48.270
It couldn't be...

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.330
Is my sister in one of those?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.140
Holly's in there?

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.540
Holly!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.240
Who's there?

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.730
Is someone there?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.030
Over there!

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.140
Sis!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.290
Professor!

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.480
It's you!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.860
Joey and Psy!

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:22.750
Why is Heroman with you?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.210
Am I dreaming?

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:29.930
See, I told you that Joey and 
Psy would come to save us!

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.620
Phew, that was close.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:38.680
We'd have been stuck in 
a capsule before long.

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:43.860
Do you have any idea how worried 
we were about you? Sheesh...

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.440
Sorry for taking so long.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.600
Why'd you come to save us?

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.860
You're just putting yourself in more danger.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.240
I guess I get my fearlessness from you, Sis.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.500
Idiot.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.720
The freak's here!

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.420
Professor Denton, take care of my sister!

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:13.920
Okay, got it!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:14.930
Joey...

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.520
Over here!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.190
Hey!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.910
Let me go!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.030
Joey!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.510
Joey!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.270
Heroman...

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:38.490
Attack!

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.350
Heroman...

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.350
Blast!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.040
I knew it! It's not Will!

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:53.900
Heroman!

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:04.710
There's another one, damn it?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.950
It's hard to fight here, I'm 
worried about a cave in!

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:10.540
Let's follow the plan and lead them outside!

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:13.530
Heroman, over here!

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:30.840
Psy!

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.590
Think you can catch me, you monster?

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.540
I'll lead you straight to your grave!

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.190
Psy's in danger!

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:10.690
If I don't do something 
about this guy quick...

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.390
What's the matter, monster? 
Follow me, damn it!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.760
Touchdown...

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.320
I'm gonna score a touchdown!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:57.620
I... can still run!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.060
And that's a touchdown!

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:12.510
Fire!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.350
Good.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.630
It's a Skrugg! Keep shooting!

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.820
Joey, Heroman!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.200
Heroman...

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.540
Finish!

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.910
Psy, are you okay?

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.540
Man, I suck...

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.970
I tripped up again in the clutch...

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:16.520
That's not true. You're 
the one that stopped him.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.220
It's happened again...

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.400
Like it did with Dad...

00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.600
This place is cursed.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.370
That accident was here?

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:39.790
And yet... Even though I 
should have protected him...

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:41.530
I couldn't do anything...

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.090
I'm a terrible sister.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:46.380
You shouldn't be so disappointed in yourself.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:50.250
Maybe you should believe in 
their strength a bit more?

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.630
See?

00:20:58.550 --> 00:20:59.850
It's them...

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:03.510
We're back, Sis.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.350
Sorry for making you worry.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:06.910
Ow!

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:12.090
Joey, Psy, thank you...

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:19.700
Um...

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:21.630
Sis?

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:24.930
You see...

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:29.690
Before that... Since when did you 
and Heroman get to be friends?

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.100
Introduce me, man!

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.620
Do you remember me?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:37.020
It must be fate that we can meet again!

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:41.060
I'll give you my number! If 
you're ever in trouble...

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:44.780
I thought she'd give turn it down 
a notch after going through that...

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.030
Nothing's too much for my sister.

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:49.970
But, that's what's great about her.

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:52.170
Psy?

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.000
What's the matter?

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.660
Psy!

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:32.400
<b>I want to get to know you better,</b>

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.490
<b>to go at each other with our true feelings.</b>

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:41.830
<b>Your tears and smile are both here.</b>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.260
<b>No matter how hard it is, I won't be scared any more.</b>

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:49.320
<b>With both of us, we can go anywhere.</b>

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:54.760
<b>Since you're the one who taught me that I'm not alone.</b>

00:22:54.760 --> 00:23:02.450
<b>Every time I mutter the words "I was born to meet you"</b>

00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:07.490
<b>my unease disappears, and my heart burns stronger.</b>

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:14.440
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:14.880 --> 00:23:19.300
<b>Carve out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>I can't move away from here.</b>

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:28.060
<b>Because I live feeling the same heartbeat.</b>

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.280
<b>I want to protect you to the very last,</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.680
<b>to protect the promise built up.</b>

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:40.080
<b>Thank you. We'll go on together with a sign only we understand.</b>

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:45.810
<b>We are carving out this irreplaceable time!</b>

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:52.860
On the next Heroman:

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:56.410
I looked up to the hero that 
Mom always talked about.

00:23:57.030 --> 00:23:58.760
But, my sister...

00:23:58.760 --> 00:24:05.610
Joey begins to worry about the danger 
he's placed his sister and friends in.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:11.700
Looking for the answer, Joey searches the 
feelings of the past, present, and future.

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:15.760
Next time on Heroman #22: Memories.

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:18.700
Heroman... Attack!
